The asynckb project changes the Python distribution, import namespace and
extension module names, adds KingbaseES MySQL/Oracle/SQL Server compatibility,
and provides the kingbase+asynckb SQLAlchemy entry point. Adaptation areas
include mode initialization, parameter binding, protocol handling, type/OID
discovery and codecs, transaction commands, statement lifecycle, connection
pool integration, authentication/MAC information, and ORM dialect integration.
See CHANGELOG.md and UPSTREAM.md. This notice is not a substitute for the
modified-file notices required by Apache License 2.0 Section 4(b).

